            <ArticleTitle>Hourly rounding is key contributor to patient-centered care at high-performing hospitals.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>109-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>According to new findings, hospitals with the highest HCAHPS scores suggest that hourly rounding on patients is one of the best ways to elevate the patient experience. In a survey of top-performing hospitals, 83% reported they employed the practice of regular nurse rounding on patients, and 62% employed leadership rounding. When rounding on patients, experts suggest nurses should always consider pain, the plan of care, and duration, or &quot;PPD&quot;.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
